; expect 6
; `restrict(no-untrapped)` over a body that divides integers through
; the checked call and a body that divides floats raw, run rather than
; only checked. Raw `/` on `Int` would be refused with no fix but the
; checked one; `/` on `Float` lowers to `fdiv` with no integer trap to
; require, while the fix the diagnostic would name - `divChecked`,
; `(-> Int Int (Result Int Error))` - does not typecheck against one.
;
; A RUN and not a check, because the exemption is a checker change on
; nodes the emitter also reads: 7 divided checked is 3, and 7.0
; halved raw truncates to 3.
;
; THE TAG IS ON THE `fn` AND NOT THE `::`, deliberately.
; `check-restrictions.sh` section 1 rewrites every blank line above a
; column-0 `(::` or `fn` in this directory into
; `;@axiom:restrict(no-foreign)` and requires the AXSYM rows to match
; afterwards but for one `#restrict=` field - except where a declaration
; already carries one, which the sweep leaves alone. A second tag above
; the signature would add a SECOND field and the comparison would see a
; row that moved; the tag on the `fn` tells the sweep this declaration
; is already claimed, and the row is the same either way.
(import Err)

(:: half (-> Int Int))
;@axiom:restrict(no-untrapped)
(fn (half n)
  (unwrapOr (divChecked n 2) 0))

(:: fhalf (-> Float Float))
;@axiom:restrict(no-untrapped)
(fn (fhalf x)
  (/ x 2.0))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (+ (half 7) (__floatToInt (fhalf 7.0))))
